@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+# Plan
+
+1. Make retained orders independently readable by changing the single-order fetch query to use left fetch joins for optional order relations, while preserving the existing scalar customer id, email, billing, and delivery data.
+2. Change the admin customer-order endpoint to query orders by the requested stored customer id even when the customer row no longer exists. Populate the response customer only when the account still exists, leaving it absent for retained historical orders.
+3. Repair order-list pagination and metadata: use a mathematically correct ceiling page count, keep matching totals on empty pages, return an empty order collection rather than a null/zero-total response, and ensure filtered queries remain constrained to the merchant when name/phone OR clauses are used.
+4. Preserve the existing delete and registration model so a newly registered customer gets a new id and cannot inherit old orders; add focused regression tests where the project’s test setup supports them.
+5. Build the affected Maven modules and run the relevant unit/integration test commands, recording any environment limitations in the final verification line.
+
